* How do we use "react-router"?
  - In "main.jsx", wrap our "<App/>" with "<BrowserRouter/>"

  - Make sure to run "import { BrowserRouter } from 'react-router';
"

  - Then in "App.jsx" , import "Routes"

  - "import { Routes } from 'react-router';"

* "<Routes>" = tells React all the pages that are in our website.

  - To ADD a page to our website, we will use a component called "<Route>"

  - Route = a page.

  - "import { Routes, Route } from 'react-router';"

  - Add "<Route>" inside "<Routes>".

  - Give "<Route>", 2 props. --> 
    - path = tells React URL path of the page.
      - EX: "/checkout"

    - element = tells React which element or component to display.

  - EX: When we go to the URL path "/", the HomePage gets displayed.
    "
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<HomePage/>}></Route>
      </Routes>
    "

* Single Page Application(SPA) = we only have 1 HTML file shared by all our pages.
  - We instead use React to create MULTIPLE pages.

  - EX: "index.html" shared by all of our pages, reducing repetition.

* "<Route index element={<HomePage/>}></Route>" is a shortcut for the following.
  - "<Route path="/" element={<HomePage/>}></Route> "

* "Components" folder is for shared components.
  - EX: "Header.jsx"

* "Pages" folder is for components specific to a page.

* Link elements (<a>) by default reload the page.

* We don't need to reload pages, we can use JavaScript to switch between pages.
  - React-Router provides a component for this: "<Link>"

  - "import { Link } from 'react-router';"

  - "<Link>" = component that lets us go to another page without reloading.

  - Faster since we can switch to another page WITHOUT reloading.

